==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{der|fo|non|ætla}}, from {{der|fo|gem-pro|*ahtalōną||to strive, think}}, from {{der|fo|ine-pro|*ok-||to think, intend, purpose}}. Landt 1800<ref>Jørgen Landt: ''Forsøg til en Beskrivelse over Færøerne''. Copenhagen 1800, reprinted 1965. (p. 249)</ref> mentions it as typical Faroese in contrast to Danish ''[[tænke]], [[slutte]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|fo|[ˈatla]}} (''also in [[Suðuroy]]'')

===Verb===
{{fo-verb|ætlaði|ætlað}}

# to [[plan]], to [[intend]]
# to [[think]]

====Conjugation====
{{fo-conj-30|ætl}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|fo|ætlan}} (plan, intention)

