==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|ætla}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*ahtalōną||to strive, think}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*ok-||to think, intend, purpose}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈaihtla/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|aihtla|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|ætlaði|ætlað}}

# to [[intend]], to [[plan]], to [[mean]] to, be [[going to]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég '''ætlaði''' ekki að særa þig.|I didn't '''mean''' to hurt you.}}
#: {{ux|is|Hún '''ætlaði''' alltaf að passa upp á hann.|She was always '''going to''' keep an eye on him.}}
#: {{ux|is|Hættu þessu, asninn þinn! Ég '''ætlaði''' að sitja þarna!|Stop that, you idiot! I was '''going''' to sit there!}}
# to intend to [[go]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég '''ætla''' heim!|I'm '''going''' home!}}
# {{lb|is|of inanimate things, happenings, etc.|or|impersonal}} to be [[going to]] (indicating a likely course of events)
#: {{ux|is|það '''ætlar''' að rigna|it's '''going''' to rain}}
# to [[think]], to [[believe]], [[suppose]], be of the opinion (that)
#: {{ux|is|Farið er að skýja, og '''ætla''' ég að fljótlega byrji að rigna.|It is getting cloudy, and I '''think''' it will soon start raining.}}
# {{lb|is|ditransitive}} to believe (something) (of someone)
# {{lb|is|ditransitive}} to [[intend]] (someone) (to do something)
# {{lb|is|present subjunctive}} to [[wonder]], to [[suppose]]
#: {{ux|is|Hvað '''ætli''' forsetinn sé að gera núna?|I '''wonder''' what the president is doing now.}}
#: {{ux|is|Átt þú ekki að vera í skólanum?'' — '''''Ætli''' það ekki.|Aren't you supposed to be at school? — I '''suppose''' so.}}

====Usage notes====
* The verb ''ætla'' is an [[auxiliary verb]] much used in Icelandic.
*: {{ux|is|Ég '''ætla''' að fara í [[bíó]].|I am going (I '''intend''' to go) to the [[cinema]].}}
* Also used to ask for something in stores.
*: {{ux|is|Ég '''ætla''' að fá eina [[kók]].|One Coke, please. (I '''intend''' to have one [[Coke]].)}}

